# `deno fmt` emits LF and reports a CRLF file as "Text differed by line endings", while a git
# running with core.autocrlf=true (this machine's, when this was written) hands out CRLF on every
# checkout. Those two
# fight each other: formatting the tree fixes `deno fmt --check` only until the next checkout
# re-introduces CRLF.
#
# Pinning eol=lf settles it — the blobs are stored as LF either way, so this only stops the
# checkout filter from converting them back to CRLF. Wildcard first (workspace Tooling rule 7,
# 2026-10-26): it used to cover `*.ts` only, so Markdown, JSON and YAML still checked out CRLF.
# Exceptions follow the wildcard, because the last matching line wins.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The sample reports are fixtures that the conservation check reads back byte for byte. Leave
# their line endings exactly as SkyCiv emitted them rather than letting a checkout rewrite them.
tests/HTMLFilesToBeCompiled/*.html -text
